@startuml
title Classroom Rover - complete RAG flow\nRead from top to bottom: time flows downward
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFBF7
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
<style>
participant {
  Padding 26
}
</style>
skinparam BoxPadding 18
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #526B55
  LifeLineBorderColor #B3BEAC
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F0F2E9
  ParticipantBorderColor #8DA17E
  ActorBorderColor #526B55
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #C5D0BB
  DividerBackgroundColor #E7EDDE
  DividerBorderColor #B4C4A4
}
hide footbox
actor "Student / user" as user
participant "<size:22><&browser></size>\nBrowser frontend\nReact chat" as frontend
box "Server-side code and local data" #F1F5EB
  participant "<size:22><&cog></size>\nBackend\nPOST /api/chat" as backend
  participant "<size:22><&terminal></size>\nIndexing script\nindex-manual.ts" as indexing
  database "Local vector index\nindex.json" as index
end box
box "OpenAI API" #EEF2FB
  participant "<size:22><&grid-two-up></size>\nEmbedding model\ntext-embedding-3-small" as embedding
  participant "<size:22><&lightbulb></size>\nLanguage model\ngpt-6-luna" as llm
end box

== 0. Prepare the manual - before using the chat ==
note over indexing,index
  Run npm run index:manual initially and after manual changes.
  This preparation is separate from each question.
end note
opt Index is missing or the manual / embedding model changed
  activate indexing
  indexing -> indexing : Read data/manual.md\nSplit into titled chunks and hash document
  indexing -> embedding : Send section titles + paragraph text\nRequest an embedding for each chunk
  activate embedding
  embedding --> indexing : One numerical vector per chunk
  deactivate embedding
  indexing -> index : Save text, source IDs, vectors,\nmodel and manual hash in index.json
  deactivate indexing
end

== 1. Ask a question ==
user -> frontend : Type a question and press Send
frontend -> backend : POST /api/chat\n{ question }
activate backend
backend -> backend : Validate input\nRead current manual fingerprint
backend -> index : Load index and validate\nmanual hash + embedding model
index --> backend : Chunk text, IDs and stored vectors

== 2. Find relevant manual sections ==
backend -> embedding : Embed the question
activate embedding
embedding --> backend : Question vector
deactivate embedding
backend -> backend : Compare vectors with cosine similarity\nFocused: top 3; multi-topic: cover headings\nOverview: all sections within budget

== 3. Generate a grounded answer ==
backend -> llm : Instructions + question\n+ retrieved excerpts
activate llm
llm --> backend : Structured answer\nSupport status + cited source IDs
deactivate llm
backend -> backend : Validate output and source IDs\nUse fixed abstention if unsupported

== 4. Show the result ==
backend --> frontend : JSON: answer, status, sources\nand cited source IDs
deactivate backend
frontend --> user : Display answer and expandable sources

note over frontend,backend
  The browser communicates with our backend.
  The API key and OpenAI calls stay on the server.
end note
@enduml
